---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: sample date. Draft wording for the demo; the final page is reviewed before the switch-over.</p>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We collect only what the site needs to run: your Western email to sign you in, and what you type into a form.</li>
    <li>No advertising, no analytics, no tracking cookies. We never sell your data or use it to train AI.</li>
    <li>The database is in Canada. Backups are in Toronto.</li>
    <li>Ask <a href="mailto:hippoit@uwo.ca">hippoit@uwo.ca</a> to correct or delete your information.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The Hippocratic Council, through its IT Director, at hippoit@uwo.ca.</p>
  <h2>2. What is collected</h2>
  <p>Your account (email, role, sign-in times); what each form asks for; club pages; and, automatically, only the sign-in session cookie and short-lived server logs.</p>
  <h2>3. Who can see it</h2>
  <p>You; the council role that handles each form (for example, the booking admins see booking requests); site admins; and the public, for club pages. Exec emails appear on a club page only if that exec opts in.</p>
  <h2>4. Instagram</h2>
  <p>Club pages load nothing from Instagram until you choose "Show recent Instagram posts".</p>
  <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Email hippoit@uwo.ca to correct or delete your information. You can also complain to the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.</p>
  <p class="demo-note">Demo: this demo stores nothing on any server. Everything you do here stays in this browser until you choose Reset demo.</p>
</Base>
